    "created_at": "2015-09-21T14:43:42Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-09-21T14:43:42Z",
    "body": "I don't think we should allow `<a>` in places where `<a href>` is not allowed -- after all, it's a \"placeholder for where a link might otherwise have been placed\". Also `<a><a>` does not parse well.\n\nNote that content models are only authoring conformance criteria, it doesn't affect implementors.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
