    "created_at": "2015-09-21T19:42:25Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-09-21T19:42:25Z",
    "body": "OK. My knee-jerk reaction is that the spec shouldn't have impl requirements that hook into an authoring requirement concept. Although if it does the right thing except for href-less `a`, I suppose it is practical. But does it? How does `<video>` sans `controls` work, if the user right-clicks the video and shows the controls? It's still not \"interactive content\", but it behaves the same as `<video controls>`, which is.\n\nIf we do make this change, then the content model of `a` also needs to change to not allow descendant `a` elements.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
